      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their cited evidence. Tier assignments are correct: stated claims draw from policy text, measurable claims from parliamentary/NHS sources, projected claims from analyst bodies. The claim that lower-income patients are 'hit hardest' by the 96.9% failure rate (E35) goes slightly beyond what the quote alone says, but the broader evidence base (E25, E26) supports the inference and it is not stated as a direct quote-entailed fact. Magnitude 'minor' and confidence 'moderate' are appropriately conservative given the capacity-constraint evidence. No party identity or motive attribution detected. Direction 'improves' is supported by claims on the distributional benefit side; no false balance issue since the verdict does not claim 'mixed'. No lever leakage \u2014 the verdict judges distributional dental access effects on O14, not the policy mechanism for its own sake."
